108.m:
Brahmā said:
Hearing the word 'Ilā', that king was overwhelmed with rage;
rebuking the yakṣiṇī, he asked her again about the doe.

109.m:
Brahmā said:
Hari dispatched his discus to slay the lord of spirits;
the lord of spirits swallowed that discus even as it came rushing.

Brahmā said:
Then the Blessed One, bearer of the conch, discus, and mace, was pleased;
he said to them: "For what purpose have you all come? I shall do that."

Brahmā said:
Then, when the gods had gone, Viṣṇu set out for the sake of the discus;
going to the Godāvarī, he commenced worship of Śambhu.
